Z||000000||KRMFiero||03-26-2001||03:50 PM||||Well people have been on the topic of changing gears in 5 speeds and 4 speeds,    what about my Automatic? I'm putting the 4.5L caddy in, I would like more speed then acceleration if possible. is there any transmitions i could get gears for? any transmition a direct bolt in? where can i get a shift kit?    how hard is it to change gears? any one know any websites on how to do it?<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red)<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||03-26-2001||05:39 PM||||I'll be the first to admit I know $hit about automatic trannys, and even less on any GM automatic tranny.<BR>But I think with only three gears to begin with, you will find a lot of "open space" where you're just not in the powerband at speeds if you change sets. I would look into a 4T60 or similar, at least something with 4 speeds. I don't know how much work that is, TK probably knows. It still amazes me how long it took GM to get more than a 3 speed FWD automatic to market.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-26-2001||08:24 PM||||It is easier to change the tranny then try to change the final drive in it. You would likely need to do a rebuild at the same time in order for it to last since you'll be disturbing the entire guts to get to the finals.||||reg||1
